# Services & Repositories

## Services (`src/lib/services/*.service.ts`)

- Contain business logic, authorization checks, and orchestration.
- Call repositories for persistence — never import Mongoose models directly.
- Use `withTransaction()` from `@/lib/db` for multi-step writes.
- Throw typed errors from `@/lib/errors`: `NotFoundError`, `ForbiddenError`, etc.
- Use `logger` from `@/lib/logger` for structured logging.
- Use `audit()` for important actions (purchases, status changes).

```typescript
export const beatService = {
  async create(input: CreateBeatInput, producerId: string): Promise<IBeat> {
    return withTransaction(async (session) => {
      const beat = await beatRepository.create({ ...input, producerId }, { session });
      await licenseRepository.createDefaults(beat._id.toString(), producerId, { session });
      return beat;
    });
  },
};
```

## Repositories (`src/lib/repositories/*.repository.ts`)

- Handle persistence only — no business rules.
- Always call `await connectDB()` before queries.
- Accept optional `{ session }` parameter for transactions.
- Return plain objects (`.lean()`) when possible for performance.

```typescript
export const beatRepository = {
  async findById(id: string) {
    await connectDB();
    return Beat.findById(id).lean<IBeat>();
  },
};
```
